62eda0deb78a49dd1b16c535fceb7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9a3fbb5491c62eda0deb78a49dd1b16c535fceb7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued July 29 at 2:45PM MDT until July 29 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Elbert County in east central Colorado...\nSoutheastern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nDouglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 545 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 245 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 1.5 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nMiddle Garber Creek, Rainbow Creek, Jackson Creek, Garber Creek,\nCook Creek, East Cherry Creek, West Creek, Indian Creek, Deep\nCreek, Spring Creek, Camp Creek, Gove Creek, Murphy Creek, Newlin\nGulch, East Plum Creek, Sugar Creek, Trout Creek, Horse Creek,\nCherry Creek, Bear Creek, Carpenter Creek, Big Dry Creek, Piney\nCreek, Running Creek, North Garber Creek, Pine Creek, Coal Creek,\nKinney Creek, West Toll Gate Creek, Willow Creek, Plum Creek,\nAntelope Creek, Bayou Gulch, First Creek, Watson Park Creek, Dry\nGulch, Happy Canyon Creek, Lake Gulch, South Platte River and\nEast Toll Gate Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1\ninch are expected over the area. This additional rain will result\nin minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthern Aurora, eastern Centennial, Castle Rock, Parker, Lone\nTree, Larkspur, Castle Pines, Franktown, Sedalia, The Pinery,\nPerry Park, Ponderosa Park, Devil's Head, Arapahoe Park,\nFoxfield, Castlewood Canyon and Shamballa.","ends":"2026-07-29T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T20:56:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 292056 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 256 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and thunderstorms likely across the high terrain in the late morning, shifting to the plains by the afternoon. - Strong storms could produce localized flash flooding, particularly for the burn scar and areas along and east of the southern I-25 Corr","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T21:12:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight and Thursday... Localized heavy rainfall may lead to flash flooding over the burn scars this afternoon and evening, as well as over areas that also received rainfall Tuesday afternoon. Shower and thunderstorm activity will diminish around 2100 MDT, although a few weak storms may linger until a bit later in the evening, particularly over the mountains and easternmost Colorado ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ccr01","station_name":"Cherry Creek Reservoir","distance_km":11.5,"soil_temp_5cm_f":88.34,"soil_temp_15cm_f":87.71,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":10.72,"wind_speed_mph":7.08,"air_temp_f":69.42,"relative_humidity":0.721,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/ccr01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KAPA","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KAPA 292153Z 21013G25KT 7SM -TSRA BKN070CB BKN090 OVC110 21/17 A3017 RMK AO2 PK WND 20028/2054 WSHFT 2040 SLP152 FRQ LTGICCG OHD TS OHD MOV NE P0000 T02060167","temp_f":69,"wind_dir":2